---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../../lib/config";
---
<Legal title="About our AI receptionist" description="Our receptionist is an AI. Here's what that means, and how call and chat data is handled." updated="[DATE]">
  <div class="mb-8 rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900" data-placeholder>
    <strong>Draft.</strong> Items in [square brackets] must be filled in before launch.
  </div>

  <h2>It's an AI, and it says so</h2>
  <p>
    When you call or chat with a business that uses Prezence Voice (including Prezence itself), you are talking to an
    <strong>AI assistant</strong>, not a person. It tells you this at the start of every call and chat.
    If you'd prefer to speak to a person, just say so and it will take a message or pass you on where the business has set that up.
  </p>

  <h2>What it can and can't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It can answer common questions using information the business gave us (services, prices, opening hours).</li>
    <li>It can take messages and booking requests and pass them to the business.</li>
    <li>It can make mistakes. Important details (prices, appointments) are confirmed by the business.</li>
    <li>It will never ask for card numbers, passwords or other sensitive details. Please don't share them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we record</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Calls:</strong> [whether calls are recorded], a written transcript, and the caller's phone number.</li>
    <li><strong>Chats:</strong> the messages you type and a random session ID. We don't use advertising cookies in the chat.</li>
    <li><strong>Summaries:</strong> a short summary of each call or chat is sent to the business so they can follow up.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it's used</h2>
  <p>
    Call and chat data is used to answer you, to pass your message to the business, and to fix problems with the service.
    The text of the conversation is processed by our AI provider to generate replies. [Confirm the provider's data use and retention terms.]
    We don't sell this data.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can see it</h2>
  <p>The business you contacted, and Prezence staff who need it to run and support the service.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>[Recordings: X days. Transcripts and summaries: X months.] After that it is deleted.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of your call or chat data, or ask us to delete it, by emailing
    <a class="underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. See our <a class="underline" href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a> for more.
  </p>
</Legal>
